// ============================================================
// CHAIN EXAMPLE (inlined) — one legal composition of the kernels + rollup base
//
// Order: init -> inner -> reset -> inner -> reset-tail-to-public
//        -> hiding-to-public -> rollup-tx-base-public
//
// NOT COMPILABLE and NOT a single circuit. Each stage is a separate proof;
// stages are joined by the CHONK databus (return_data of one == call_data of
// the next) and recursive verification, both enforced by barretenberg, NOT by
// any Noir assert here. The `// JOIN` comments mark those hand-offs.
//
// PROVER FREEDOM: the prover chooses the composition — how many inner/reset
// iterations, which batch/reset variants, and the ordering (within the VK
// allow-lists). This file shows ONE instance; the semantic output must be
// identical across all legal compositions, so do not read this shape as the
// only one. (reset shown is the MAX-size variant.)
//
// Use for cross-circuit (P8) reading: trace a value's lifecycle across folds,
// and look for a check that lives 'between' circuits and is owned by none.
// Verify any finding against the real per-circuit source/artifacts.
// ============================================================

